agefiles and srd059-version, I should focus on cmd/version/ as the actual implementation target. I'm also noting which package contracts are already provided—testutils, sys, format, hashutil, and sizeparse—so I can factor those into what still needs to be implemented.\n\nThe build order is becoming clearer: testutils first since it has no dependencies, then format which depends on the already-implemented sys, then hashutil with no package dependencies, and finally cmd/version/. I'm checking the requirement states to understand the weights and readiness of each component, though I don't have the full weight details yet.\n\nSince the default weight is 1 per requirement and I need to keep each task under 4 requirements total, I should also remember that contract tasks need to come before implementation tasks for new packages—those define the exported types and function signatures as stubs first. I'm hitting the 4-task limit, so I need to prioritize carefully. The constraint requires separate contract and implementation tasks, which means I can only cover two packages fully. Given the dependencies, testutils needs to come first since other packages depend on it, followed by format since it's needed by the ls and du commands. That leaves me with testutils contract, testutils implementation, format contract, and format implementation as my four tasks.\n\nNow I'm checking what the testutils contract actually requires—looking at the DiffTest struct, Normalizer function type, and the key functions like RunDiffTests and ComposeNormalizers that need to be defined. So the missing SRDs from requirement_states might not have \"ready\" status requirements, which would explain why they're absent—and that could mean I shouldn't be proposing tasks for format, testutils, and hashutil if their requirements aren't actually ready to be worked on. they're in a \"not ready\" state) or they don't have requirement states at all. Given that these packages show \"not started\" in code_status a